<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 580 0 R
/T (    At SoCal Showdown, we reached over 250 elementary and middle school students through targeted STEM outreach. We facilitated  four hands-on activities which included cookie carving to introduce precision and design concepts, spaghetti towers to promote structural thinking and teamwork, and robot driving to simulate FTC competition skills from our team drivers. These activities increased participants' confidence, communication skills, and interest in FIRST programs, helping to inspire sustained engagement  STEM fields. Cookie Carving: Students would carve chocolate chips out of cookies then eat it after. Spaghetti tower: We challenged students to create a 2 feet tall tower out of spaghetti and marshmallow in two minutes. Origami challenge: We would teach students how to make origami then If students could remake the origami, they get candy.)
/E (    At SoCal Showdown, we reached over 250 elementary and middle school students through targeted STEM outreach. We facilitated  four hands-on activities which included cookie carving to introduce precision and design concepts, spaghetti towers to promote structural thinking and teamwork, and robot driving to simulate FTC competition skills from our team drivers. These activities increased participants' confidence, communication skills, and interest in FIRST programs, helping to inspire sustained engagement  STEM fields. Cookie Carving: Students would carve chocolate chips out of cookies then eat it after. Spaghetti tower: We challenged students to create a 2 feet tall tower out of spaghetti and marshmallow in two minutes. Origami challenge: We would teach students how to make origami then If students could remake the origami, they get candy.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
