1370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 585 0 R
/E (Before designing our Shooter, we outlined a key requirement: the ability to shoot from the Far Launch Zone at a fixed angle.  We first created a simple diagram to represent our goal. Then, using  Projectile Kinematic Equations, we modeled a 3 meters \(XGoal\) shooting distance with a goal height of 0.984 meters \(HGoal\), accounting for robot height of 0.238 Meters \(HBot\).  By expressing Ymax as the height of the ball need to rise, which calculated by subtracting the height of the goal from the height of the robot. Xmax represents the minimum distance from the goal. We simulated the solution in Desmos, resulting in optimal launch angle of 30.2 degree for consistent scoring from 3 Meters!)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
